statement:
The string `s` uses only the letters `'a'`, `'b'` and `'c'`. One operation cuts a block off the front of `s` and a block off the back of `s` at the same time, where:

- the front block is non-empty and made of one repeated character;
- the back block is non-empty and made of one repeated character;
- both blocks use the same character;
- the two blocks share no position of the string.

You may apply the operation any number of times, including zero. Return the shortest length `s` can be brought down to.

validator:
function validate([s]) {
  if (typeof s !== 'string' || s.length < 1 || s.length > 100000) return 's needs 1 to 10^5 characters.';
  if (!/^[abc]+$/.test(s)) return 's may only contain a, b and c.';
  return null;
}

